The Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm efficiently finds the majority element (appearing more than ⌊n/2⌋ times) in O(n) time and O(1) space. Here’s the correct implementation:

```python
def find_majority_element(arr):
    candidate = None
    count = 0
    for num in arr:
        if count == 0:
            candidate = num
        count += (1 if num == candidate else -1)
    # Verify if the candidate is indeed the majority element
    if arr.count(candidate) > len(arr) // 2:
        return candidate
    return None
```

